# Evidence-Aware Knowledge & Retrieval Architecture for AI-Assisted JSEA
## Research Roadmap: PSI Integration into Package 1B & 2B

> **Role assumed:** Deep-research architect for evidence-aware knowledge and retrieval systems  
> **Scope:** Chemical and petrochemical process facilities  
> **Access date:** 2026-08-15  
> **Research basis:** OSHA 29 CFR 1910.119, EPA RMP 40 CFR Part 68, CCPS RBPS, UK HSE HSG250/HSG253, ISO 45001, ISO 14001, Thailand Hazardous Substance Act B.E. 2535, plus full audit of Package 1B and 2B

---

## Executive Summary

Package 1B and 2B are well-designed occupational hazard discovery and safeguard challenge tools. Their current knowledge stack is **Category A competent**: it covers energy families, environmental pathways, hierarchy of controls, dependency patterns, and evidence discipline. However, when deployed in **chemical or petrochemical process facilities**, both packages operate with a structural blind spot: they are agnostic to Process Safety Information (PSI) — the technical bedrock that determines whether a task-level JSEA is meaningful or dangerously incomplete.

In process industries, most catastrophic incidents (Baker Panel, Texas City; Bhopal; Piper Alpha; Deepwater Horizon; IEAT incidents in Thailand) are not caused by occupational ergonomics failures. They are caused by **loss of primary containment (LOPC)** of energetic or toxic materials, combined with inadequate understanding of process conditions, equipment state, and protection layer integrity at the moment of task execution.

The gap is not in the JSEA methodology — it is in the **knowledge the AI brings to the conversation before and during the analysis**.

**This roadmap proposes a three-layer extension:**
1. **PSI Awareness Layer** — static knowledge of what PSI is, what it contains, and why its absence is a `CRITICAL EVIDENCE_GAP`
2. **PSI Retrieval Layer** — runtime prompting and evidence routing to extract PSI from organizational sources
3. **PSI Integration Layer** — encoding PSI into the hazard-analysis and safeguard-challenge workflows at the right decision points

