## Part 2: "AI Should Know / Retrieve / Ask / Never Infer" Matrix

> Classification: **KNOW** = pre-encoded in static reference | **RETRIEVE** = request from organizational/field sources | **ASK** = formulate a specific question to the user/competent person | **NEVER INFER** = prohibited assumption

### 2.1 Chemical & Process Material Domain

| Topic | KNOW | RETRIEVE | ASK | NEVER INFER |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Generic chemical hazard categories (toxic/flammable/corrosive) | ✅ HE-06 | — | — | — |
| Specific chemical identity in this system | Partial (SDS principles) | ✅ SDS, Stream Tables, Lab Analyses | "What substances and mixtures are confirmed in this equipment?" | Assume water/air is the only content |
| Mixture composition and trace contaminants | — | ✅ Stream Analysis, Operating Manual | "Are there trace toxic components (H₂S, Benzene, Mercury, HF)?" | That bulk chemical = total hazard |
| Flash point vs. operating temperature comparison | Know principle | ✅ SDS Flash Point + Operating T data | "Is operating temperature above Flash Point?" | That liquid is non-flammable without data |
| Reactivity / incompatibility with cleaning agents | Know principle | ✅ SDS Section 7, Compatibility Matrix | "What cleaning/flushing media will be used? Is it compatible?" | Compatibility is acceptable |
| Pyrophoric iron sulfide potential | Know principle (sour service indicator) | ✅ MI records, sour-service history | "Is this equipment in sour (H₂S) service? Has decontamination been completed and verified?" | FeS is absent without evidence |
| Phase behavior under depressurization | Know principle (flashing) | ✅ PFD, P&T data | "Will material flash to vapor when pressure is released?" | No flash risk without checking |
| Cryogenic embrittlement risk | Know principle | ✅ Equipment Datasheets, MOC | "Is rapid blowdown or auto-refrigeration possible? What is the minimum design temperature?" | Carbon steel is adequate without check |
| Maximum intended inventory | — | ✅ PFD, Mass Balance | Required for consequence estimation | Inventory is small |

### 2.2 Process Technology & Conditions Domain

| Topic | KNOW | RETRIEVE | ASK | NEVER INFER |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Concept of Safe Operating Limits | ✅ Know | ✅ SOL sheets, Operating Manuals | "What are the Upper and Lower Safe Limits for P/T/Level/Flow for affected equipment?" | Current conditions are within limits |
| Consequence of deviations from Safe Envelope | Know principle | ✅ PHA/HAZOP consequence register | "Has this deviation scenario been covered in PHA?" | Deviation will be manageable |
| Current operating P and T (real-time) | — | ✅ DCS/Control Room + Field Gauge | "What is current operating pressure and temperature? Who confirms zero-energy state?" | P = 0 without field confirmation |
| Process chemistry (exothermic reactions, catalyst sensitivity) | Know principle | ✅ Operating Manual, PHA records | "Is there any catalyst or reactive chemistry that could be initiated by this task?" | Task is inert to process chemistry |
| MOC status and open items | — | ✅ MOC Register | "Are there open MOC items that affect the scope of this task?" | No open MOC items |
| Temporary configuration deviations | — | ✅ Bypass register, Shift logbook | "Are there any temporary bypasses, jumpers, or non-standard configurations currently in place?" | Equipment is in standard configuration |

### 2.3 Equipment Domain

| Topic | KNOW | RETRIEVE | ASK | NEVER INFER |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Concept of P&ID and line numbering | ✅ Know | ✅ Current approved P&ID revision | "What is the P&ID number and revision for this equipment? Has it been field-verified against current configuration?" | P&ID is current and accurate |
| Materials of construction compatibility | Know principle | ✅ Equipment Datasheets, Line Specs | "What is the pipe/vessel material? Is it compatible with cleaning media?" | Carbon steel is acceptable |
| Relief valve and rupture disc routing | Know principle | ✅ Relief System Design, P&ID | "Where does the relief outlet route — to atmosphere, flare, or closed header?" | Relief is adequately routed |
| Interlock / SIS bypass status | Know principle | ✅ Bypass/Inhibit Register, MOC | "Are any alarms, trips, or interlocks currently inhibited or in manual mode?" | All protective systems are active |
| Hazardous area classification and equipment Ex-rating | Know concept | ✅ Area Classification Drawing, ATEX Cert. | "What is the electrical area classification at the work location? Do all electrical tools and temporary power meet Ex-rating?" | Standard tools are acceptable |
| Mechanical integrity status | Know concept | ✅ MI database, Inspection Records | "Is there any known corrosion, cracking, or temporary repair on equipment in the work boundary?" | Equipment is in good condition |
| Dead-leg and spectacle blind locations | Know concept | ✅ P&ID (reviewed), Isolation Register | "Are there dead-legs or spectacle blinds in the isolation boundary that could trap pressure?" | Isolation boundary is complete |
| Check valve position (not positive isolation) | Know principle | Must ask | "Is isolation relying on any check valves? — Check valves do NOT constitute positive isolation" | Check valve = adequate isolation |

