## Part 3: Chemical-Process JSEA Domain Map

> For each domain: **AI Pre-Knowledge** | **Runtime Retrieval** | **STOP_AND_ESCALATE Conditions** | **Competent Role**

### Domain 1: Process Chemistry and Reactivity
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Generic categories (exothermic, endothermic, polymerization, decomposition, runaway criteria)
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Process chemistry section of Operating Manual; PHA runaway scenario register; SDS Section 10 (reactivity)
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Unknown chemical identity; unverified compatibility of cleaning media; any indication of unexpected reaction or exothermic activity
- **Competent Role:** Process Engineer, Chemical Engineer, Process Safety Engineer

### Domain 2: Toxic, Flammable, and Corrosive Release Pathways
- **Pre-Knowledge:** LOPC scenarios; jet fire, pool fire, flash fire, VCE, BLEVE mechanics; H₂S IDLH = 50 ppm; LFL/UFL concept
- **Runtime Retrieval:** SDS (all materials in system); Stream composition analysis; Area toxic-gas detector map; Atmospheric dispersion consequence estimates from PHA
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** H₂S or other IDLH-concentration toxic confirmed without gas-testing evidence; flammable atmosphere without LFL measurement; unknown atmosphere in confined space
- **Competent Role:** Occupational Hygienist, Process Safety Engineer, Area HSE

### Domain 3: Isolation and Line Breaking
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Positive isolation > Double-block-and-bleed (DBB) > single valve; spectacle blind vs. spade; blind list concept; HSE HSG253 principles
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Approved Isolation Standard (site); Current Blind/Spade List (field-tagged); P&ID showing isolation point; PTW isolation certificates
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** No positive isolation confirmed for IDLH-toxic or high-pressure service; isolation relies only on check valves or remote-operated valves; blind list not current
- **Competent Role:** Isolation Authority, Mechanical Engineer, Operations Supervisor

### Domain 4: Confined Space and Atmospheric Hazards
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Oxygen deficiency < 19.5% / enrichment > 23.5%; LFL threshold (>10% LFL = prohibit hot work; >25% = suspend work); H₂S IDLH; continuous monitoring requirement; atmosphere changes during work
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Confined space classification register; Calibration records for atmospheric monitors; Rescue capability assessment; Initial and pre-entry gas test records
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Any LFL > 0 without understanding source; any H₂S above OSHA PEL without SCBA confirmation; no rescue capability verified; atmospheric monitor not calibrated
- **Competent Role:** Confined Space Supervisor, Occupational Hygienist, Rescue Team

### Domain 5: Process Control, Alarms, Interlocks, and Remote Start
- **Pre-Knowledge:** SIS concept; safety instrumented function; bypass register; permissive logic; remote/auto-start hazard
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Bypass/Inhibit Register; Cause & Effect Diagrams; P&ID showing ESD and controls; Shift log for any defeated safeguards
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Critical interlock confirmed as bypassed with no compensating measure and no MOC; remote/auto-start possibility unaddressed; unknown SIS status
- **Competent Role:** Instrumentation Engineer, Control Systems Engineer, Process Safety Engineer

### Domain 6: Pressure Relief, Vent, Flare, and Drainage
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Relief device types; open vs. closed relief system; environmental consequence of atmospheric venting; blocked relief = catastrophic failure mode
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Relief system P&ID; Car-seal-open register; Flare header pressure status; Drain destination map; Bund/dyke drainage routing
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Relief path is confirmed blocked (valve closed, no CS-O record); drain routes to open environment from toxic/flammable service
- **Competent Role:** Process Engineer, Piping Engineer, Environmental Officer

### Domain 7: Mechanical Integrity and Equipment Condition
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Corrosion allowance concept; inspection interval; fitness-for-service; temporary repair limitations; seasonal/cyclic degradation
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Inspection/Fitness-for-Service records; Corrosion monitoring data; Outstanding maintenance WOs; Temporary repair register; Last thickness survey date
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Known active corrosion at work boundary; temporary repair within work zone; inspection overdue with no fitness-for-service assessment; equipment operating above design limits
- **Competent Role:** Inspection Engineer, Corrosion Engineer, Mechanical Integrity Lead

### Domain 8: Hot Work, Ignition Sources, and Hazardous Area
- **Pre-Knowledge:** ATEX Zone 0/1/2 (IECEx/ATEX); Class I Division 1/2 (NEC/NFPA); hot work permit requirement; ignition energy thresholds; static electricity in hydrocarbon streams
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Hazardous Area Classification Drawing (current revision); Hot Work Permit; Gas test record immediately before ignition; Ex-certificate for all electrical tools
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Hot work planned in Zone 1/Class I Div 1 without confirmed gas-free atmosphere and hot work permit; non-Ex-rated equipment in classified area; no gas test within 30 minutes of hot work activity
- **Competent Role:** Electrical Engineer, Area HSE, Permit Issuing Authority

### Domain 9: SIMOPS and Cross-Unit Effects
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Shared isolation failure; conflicting energy sources; firewater availability conflict; evacuation route conflict
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Active Permit Map (current shift); SIMOPS Plan; Area Coordinator confirmation; Adjacent unit operating status
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** Permits in adjacent units create shared isolation, conflicting ignition sources, or blocked evacuation; no SIMOPS coordination confirmed
- **Competent Role:** Area Coordinator, PTW Administrator, Operations Superintendent

### Domain 10: Environmental LOPC and Off-Site Impact
- **Pre-Knowledge:** Consequence pathways (drain to soil/water/air); notification thresholds; containment capacity; firewater contamination
- **Runtime Retrieval:** Drainage destination map; Bund/dyke capacity; Environmental receptor map; Regulatory threshold list (Thailand: Hazardous Substance Act / IEAT notifications)
- **STOP_AND_ESCALATE:** LOPC could reach open drain or watercourse without bund/dyke containment; no firewater contamination plan; off-site receptor within dispersion zone
- **Competent Role:** Environmental Officer, EHS Manager, Regulator notification (DIW/IEAT as applicable)

