## Part 5: Runtime Retrieval Decision Tree

> When job type + detected hazard triggers a branch, retrieve minimum documents and ask listed questions.

### Branch 1: Hot Work Near Hydrocarbon Service

**Trigger:** Task involves sparks, flame, grinding, or heating near equipment in hydrocarbon/chemical service.

```
Required Minimum:
  - Hot Work Permit (site procedure)
  - Hazardous Area Classification Drawing (current revision)
  - Gas test result (within 30 min before ignition; continuous if Zone 1)
  - PTW and isolation certificate for affected adjacent equipment
  - ERP (fire response, muster point, extinguisher availability)
  
Conditional (if H₂S service):
  - Atmospheric gas test for H₂S as well as LFL
  - SCBA availability and training confirmation

Prohibited Assumptions:
  - Area is "normally safe" based on historical experience
  - Gas test from start of shift is still valid hours later
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Any LFL > 10% or H₂S > 1 ppm without explanation
  - No current gas test record
  - Zone 1 or Div 1 without Ex-rated equipment
  
Roles to Consult: Area HSE, Permit Issuing Authority, Electrical Engineer (if Zone 1)
```

### Branch 2: Line Breaking / Equipment Opening

**Trigger:** Task involves breaking a flange, removing a blind, opening a valve bonnet, cutting a line, or opening any pressurized/contained system.

```
Required Minimum:
  - Current P&ID (verified revision) showing isolation points
  - Blind/Spade List (field-tagged, current)
  - Positive isolation certificate
  - Depressurization and drain confirmation (field gauge at zero, drain verified)
  - Chemical content identification (SDS for all materials possible in line)
  - Decontamination/purge confirmation (if toxic or flammable)
  - PTW (Line Breaking type)
  
Conditional:
  - If sour service (H₂S): Pyrophoric iron sulfide decontamination procedure confirmation
  - If cryogenic: Low-temperature embrittlement assessment
  - If flashing liquid: Vaporization consequence estimate
  - If dead-legs suspected: P&ID markup showing dead-leg locations
  
Prohibited Assumptions:
  - DBB valve = positive isolation for IDLH-toxic or high-inventory service
  - Check valve = adequate isolation
  - Line "looks empty" = safe to open without decontamination confirmation
  - "We've done this before" = no new hazards
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Positive isolation NOT confirmed for toxic/high-pressure service → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Unknown material in line → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Trapped pressure suspected (thermal expansion, dead-leg) → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  
Roles: Isolation Authority, Process Engineer (confirm contents), Competent Person (confirm zero-energy)
```

### Branch 3: Confined Space Entry

```
Required Minimum:
  - Confined Space Classification (permit-required or not)
  - Initial atmospheric test BEFORE entry (O₂, LFL, H₂S, CO at minimum)
  - Continuous atmospheric monitoring plan
  - Rescue capability verification (trained rescuer, retrieval equipment, communication)
  - PTW (Confined Space type)
  - Ventilation plan and verification
  - Entrant/Attendant role assignment
  
Conditional:
  - If biological/microbial risk: Bioaerosol controls
  - If heat stress: Core temperature monitoring plan
  
Prohibited Assumptions:
  - Space was "gas-free yesterday"
  - A single gas test at entry is sufficient for ongoing work
  - Rescue by entry is acceptable without rescue-by-retrieval assessment
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - O₂ < 19.5% or > 23.5% → DO NOT ENTER
  - LFL > 10% → DO NOT ENTER
  - No rescue capability confirmed → DO NOT ENTER
  
Roles: Confined Space Supervisor, Occupational Hygienist, Rescue Team Lead
```

### Branch 4: Pressurized System Maintenance (Valve, Pump, Compressor, Exchanger)

```
Required Minimum:
  - Isolation scheme on P&ID
  - Isolation certificate (positive isolation for rated service)
  - Depressurization and drain confirmation
  - LOTO verification at all energy sources
  - Content identification and residue decontamination plan
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Residual pressure on gauge after isolation declared → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Unknown residue in equipment → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Relief path is blocked (no CS-O record) → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
```

### Branch 5: Chemical Transfer (Loading, Unloading, Sampling, Dosing)

```
Required Minimum:
  - SDS for both source and destination chemicals
  - Chemical compatibility check (mixing potential)
  - Earthing/bonding verification (static electricity)
  - Spill containment confirmation (bund, absorbent)
  - Atmospheric monitoring if toxic or flammable
  - PTW if required by site standard
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Chemical incompatibility with receiving vessel contents → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Earthing not confirmed for flammable liquid transfer → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
```

### Branch 6: Electrical Isolation (LOTO)

```
Required Minimum:
  - Single-line diagram or electrical drawing (current revision)
  - LOTO procedure for specific equipment
  - Voltage verification at the point of work
  - Confirmation of all energy sources (multi-energy LOTO)
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Voltage detected after LOTO declared → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Backfeed or induced voltage source identified → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
  - Unknown energy source on single-line diagram → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
```

### Branch 7: Return to Service After Maintenance (PSSR)

```
Required Minimum:
  - PSSR checklist completed
  - All blinds and spades removed (Blind List closed)
  - All temporary bypasses restored
  - Alarms and trips reinstated and tested
  - Operating procedure reviewed for any changes
  - Area HSE walk-down completed
  - Operating team briefed
  
Escalation Triggers:
  - Open items on PSSR checklist → Cannot authorize return to service
  - Any interlock not reinstated → STOP_AND_ESCALATE
```

