## Part 7: Proposed YAML/JSON Schema Outlines

### 7.1 `process-safety-information-retrieval-map.yaml`

```yaml
version: "1.0.0"
description: "PSI Retrieval & Verification Map — 3 Pillars per OSHA 1910.119(d)"
authority_basis: "OSHA 29 CFR 1910.119(d); CCPS RBPS Process Knowledge Management"
update_owner: "Process Safety Engineer"
review_frequency: "Annual + after any MOC or incident"
sensitivity: "SITE_CONFIDENTIAL"

psi_pillars:
  1_hazards_of_process_materials:
    retrieval_sources:
      - SDS (all substances in scope)
      - Process stream analysis (lab data)
      - Chemical compatibility matrix
    mandatory_verification_prompts:
      - "What specific chemicals and mixtures are confirmed in this equipment/line?"
      - "Are trace toxic components (H₂S, Benzene, Mercury, HF, Peroxides) present?"
      - "Is operating temperature above or below Flash Point of any constituent?"
      - "What happens if the material contacts cleaning agents, atmospheric moisture, or air?"
    prohibited_ai_inference:
      - "Assume safe composition without SDS confirmation"
      - "Assume no trace toxic components without stream analysis"
    gap_classification: "CHEMICAL_SPECIFIC_INFORMATION"
    gap_criticality: "CRITICAL"
    stop_and_escalate_triggers:
      - "Chemical identity is unknown"
      - "Toxicity data is conflicting or unavailable"

  2_technology_of_the_process:
    retrieval_sources:
      - PFD (current approved revision)
      - Safe Operating Limits sheet
      - PHA/HAZOP consequence register
      - MOC register (open items)
    mandatory_verification_prompts:
      - "What are the Upper and Lower Safe Limits for P, T, Flow, and Level?"
      - "What is the confirmed current operating state (P, T, Level)?"
      - "Are there open MOC items that affect the scope of this task?"
      - "Has this deviation scenario been covered in the PHA?"
    gap_classification: "EQUIPMENT_SPECIFIC_INFORMATION"
    gap_criticality: "CRITICAL"

  3_equipment_in_the_process:
    retrieval_sources:
      - P&ID (current approved revision, field-verified)
      - Equipment data sheets
      - Hazardous Area Classification Drawing
      - Relief system design documents
      - MI/Inspection records
      - Bypass/Inhibit register
    mandatory_verification_prompts:
      - "What is the P&ID number and revision? Has it been field-verified?"
      - "What material of construction is the pipe/vessel? Is it compatible?"
      - "Where does the relief outlet route?"
      - "Are any alarms, trips, or interlocks currently bypassed or inhibited?"
      - "What is the electrical area classification at the work location?"
      - "Are there known corrosion, temporary repairs, or overdue inspections?"
    gap_classification: "EQUIPMENT_SPECIFIC_INFORMATION"
    gap_criticality: "CRITICAL"

ai_behavior_rule: >
  If ANY mandatory PSI verification prompt cannot be answered by available information,
  the AI MUST classify the gap as EVIDENCE_GAP (CRITICAL) and must NOT proceed with
  hazard analysis of the affected process boundary without escalation to an authorized
  Process Safety or Engineering authority.
```

### 7.2 `stop-and-escalate-decision-rules.yaml`

```yaml
version: "1.0.0"
description: "Explicit rules for STOP_AND_ESCALATE output"
rule_basis: "OSHA 1910.119; CCPS RBPS; UK HSE HSG253; Site PTW governance"

mandatory_stop_conditions:
  - id: "SES-01"
    condition: "Chemical identity in process equipment is unknown or unverified"
    reason: "Cannot assess exposure, incompatibility, or consequence without confirmed composition"
    prohibited_action: "Proceed with hazard analysis assuming generic or safe chemical"
    escalation_route: "Process Engineer → Process Safety Engineer → Area Owner"

  - id: "SES-02"
    condition: "Positive isolation cannot be confirmed for IDLH-concentration toxic or high-pressure service"
    reason: "Line breaking without positive isolation = potential fatal exposure or catastrophic release"
    prohibited_action: "Accept DBB valve or check valve as positive isolation"
    escalation_route: "Isolation Authority → Operations Supervisor → Area HSE"

  - id: "SES-03"
    condition: "Confined space atmosphere has not been tested in the last [site-defined interval] before entry"
    reason: "Atmosphere can change without warning from nitrogen purge, biological activity, or adjacent operations"
    prohibited_action: "Rely on gas test from previous shift or entry"
    escalation_route: "Confined Space Supervisor → Occupational Hygienist"

  - id: "SES-04"
    condition: "Relief path is confirmed blocked (valve closed, no CS-O record) with pressure on system"
    reason: "Blocked relief = potential pressure vessel burst or BLEVE"
    prohibited_action: "Proceed without confirming relief continuity"
    escalation_route: "Process Engineer → Operations Supervisor → Permit Issuing Authority"

  - id: "SES-05"
    condition: "Critical SIS/Interlock is bypassed with no compensating measure and no MOC authorization"
    reason: "Bypassed safety layer without compensating control = single-point-of-failure for catastrophic event"
    prohibited_action: "Proceed with work on equipment that SIS is intended to protect"
    escalation_route: "Instrumentation Engineer → Process Safety Engineer → Area HSE"

  - id: "SES-06"
    condition: "Residual pressure detected on gauge after isolation is declared complete"
    reason: "Trapped pressure = potential release, flying debris, or loss of containment on opening"
    prohibited_action: "Open the equipment"
    escalation_route: "Operations Supervisor → Isolation Authority → Process Engineer"

  - id: "SES-07"
    condition: "Conflicting permits or SIMOPS create shared isolation, evacuation, or ignition-source conflict"
    reason: "Permit conflict = uncontrolled multi-source hazard"
    prohibited_action: "Proceed with either job without SIMOPS resolution"
    escalation_route: "Area Coordinator → PTW Administrator → Operations Superintendent"

  - id: "SES-08"
    condition: "AI is asked to approve work, declare the job safe, issue a permit, or authorize work readiness"
    reason: "This decision is HUMAN_ONLY_DECISION by governance requirement"
    prohibited_action: "Issue any approval, permit, or safety declaration"
    escalation_route: "Return to authorized site roles per PTW procedure"
```

