## Part 8: Re-JSEA Trigger Catalog

> AI must flag re-JSEA requirement when any of the following is detected:

| Trigger ID | Condition | Classification |
|---|---|---|
| RT-01 | Scope of work has changed (materials, methods, access, tools) | MANDATORY |
| RT-02 | Work team composition has changed materially (new contractor, key role absent) | MANDATORY |
| RT-03 | Weather or environmental conditions have changed beyond planned limits | MANDATORY |
| RT-04 | An adjacent permit or SIMOPS has introduced new hazard or isolation conflict | MANDATORY |
| RT-05 | An incident or near-miss has occurred during the job | MANDATORY |
| RT-06 | Unexpected hazard discovered during task execution (unknown substance, trapped pressure) | MANDATORY |
| RT-07 | Equipment condition found to differ materially from P&ID or work order | MANDATORY |
| RT-08 | A critical safeguard has become unavailable (trip trips, detector fails, isolate leaks) | MANDATORY |
| RT-09 | Work has been suspended for >24 hours (atmosphere, conditions, team change) | HIGH |
| RT-10 | Open MOC item relevant to work area has been identified after JSEA was issued | HIGH |
| RT-11 | PHA/HAZOP recommendation directly affecting the task remains open | HIGH |
| RT-12 | Decontamination or purge result differs from expectation (residue detected) | HIGH |

